usage: module-nav drivers [-h] [--json] [module]

One row per driver network (a BDeviceNetwork subclass in an -rt module): family, device, license
feature, doc module. With a module: the full anatomy of its networks (devices, point-device-ext,
proxy-ext, managers, discovery jobs, license features, doc module).

positional arguments:
  module      Submodule (modbusTcp-rt) or module directory (modbusTcp)

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  --json      JSON output

examples: drivers | drivers modbusTcp-rt | drivers niagaraDriver --json
